+
+## Secret milestone C: Fatal Exception, full endpoint
+
+The descriptor in src/data/secret-cutscene.js now contains nine sections totaling 40,000 ms. Collapse (32-36 s) extends the existing NorthStar OS scene and shared screen engine with seeded held poses, live trailing cursors, sliding tiles, gray/noise window failure, the final original dialog, underscore window and real CRT line/dot/black. Resurrection (36-40 s) uses src/fx/secret-background.js, the same material renderer called by the Secret finish: 800 ms black, pixel expansion, seeded glyph storm, six 300 ms locks, 400 ms hold and profile-limited first inversion. The dynamic invert beat and other renderer beats flush through the existing shared runtime, including the handoff's last frame.
+
+The intro's field clock advances in presentation seconds. The release hook preserves its exact last field time, first-cycle epoch and profile instead of starting another wallpaper at zero; the card finish samples that session on mount, immediately setting the 95% squircle border from the field inversion. Only the cinematic word/glyph overlay is transient. The descriptor handoff stays flipMs=400 and fadeMs=160; the cinematic occupies 40 seconds before that flip (40.4 seconds including it at Normal). The retained backdrop uses the existing scheduler, focus/idle policies and 450 ms decision exit. Recovery and the existing 500 ms skip endpoint use a seeded quiet final field without replay or reward mutation.
+
+Safe's first reversal starts after the letter hold; the second waits 4.8 presentation seconds and completes behind the card. Crossfades are 800 ms, lines are irregular/bounded, and the line motion stays 0.4 Hz. The safety rule overrides the conflicting request for two reversals inside the final second. Full keeps the faster closing cycle followed by the original Found sweep cadence, with re-entering lines blended over 300 ms to avoid an abrupt reset. Lite stays static. Both reuse A's final-output limiter and measured flash meter.
+
+Short has authored 3+3+4+3+1.5+4 = 18.5 seconds; the approximate 16-second prose is not used to shorten resurrection. Calm is four seconds, Canvas only, with a static Basic back, fade through black, static original exception, pixel/letters and gradual static-field fade. Very Low, Off and reduced motion select it and force Safe. Fast scales the shared narrative/flip to 70%, while inversion crossfade/interval limits remain measured in presentation time.
+
+The existing Mythical and Ascendant read the common profile for a small Safe-only follow-up: restrained crystal breathing, one-Hz Mythical star with compressed-time compensation, 1.8-Hz Ascendant ritual cap and attenuated existing single white envelopes. Full preserves earlier normal-play appearance. No new renderer, assets, fonts, audio or durable pull/reward logic is introduced. Runtime completion/visual acceptance, including B's post-fix avalanche and Full notice, is unverified after a setup obstruction in C's sole permitted browser session; see C-DELIVERY.md.
